SYNAPSE — LICENSE AND TERMS OF USE
Version 0.3 · Project Author: Thistle

0. GENERAL PROVISIONS
Synapse is a free project. It has always been, is, and will remain completely free of charge.

This license applies to all parts of the project:
- In-game mod (.package and .ts4script)
- Bridge application and launcher (ai_bridge.py, launcher.py, .bat files, any .exe files)
- Original presets, system prompts, configuration files, and settings
- Icons, UI design, visual assets, and graphics
- Documentation, texts, and descriptions

Distribution terms are divided into two parts:
- Creative assets (graphics, icons, UI design, texts, original prompts, presets, documentation) are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/
- Software code (mod, bridge application, launcher, scripts, executable files) is governed by the author's custom Source-Available terms set forth below. Creative Commons officially does not recommend its licenses for software; therefore, the code is licensed separately.

The permissions described in Section 1 (specifically regarding translations and user presets) constitute express individual exceptions granted by the author to the NoDerivatives condition of the CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 license and apply strictly within the scope defined in this document.

1. WHAT IS PERMITTED
- Free Redistribution. You may share the original, unmodified mod and bridge application on any websites, forums, and file-hosting services, provided all of the following conditions are met: mandatory attribution to the author (Thistle) and indication of the current version number; download access must be strictly free of charge and unmonetized; the archive and all files must be distributed in their original state without any modification or repackaging of executable files.
- Translations into Any Language. Everything is permitted for standalone translation files: early access, subscriptions, donations, and any form of monetization. No royalties to the author are required. Translation files are strictly defined as: a standalone .package file for the game installed on top of the original mod; a standalone .txt / .json localization file for the bridge application. Conditions: the translation must be distributed strictly as a separate file and must not bundle any files from the original mod or bridge; the translator must clearly state that the translation is unofficial (fan-made) and that the mod author (Thistle) is not affiliated with any fundraising for the localization; translators are solely responsible for complying with the EA Modding Policy.
- Custom Presets and Prompts. Users are permitted to create their own character/lore presets and system prompts for Synapse and share them with the community free of charge, provided they are distributed as standalone configuration/text files without including the mod's code or original files.
- Integrations and Add-ons. You may create external scripts and applications that interact with the mod's API, provided they contain no Synapse code and are distributed free of charge.
- Streaming, Videos, Reviews, and Guides. Permitted, including on monetized channels and publications, provided proper attribution is given.
- Code Inspection. Studying the project's source code (Source-Available) for educational, informational, and personal security auditing purposes is permitted.

2. WHAT IS STRICTLY PROHIBITED
- Selling the mod, bridge application, their code, any of their parts, assets, or modifications.
- Distributing the mod, bridge, or any forks thereof via paid early access, paid roles, subscriptions, or paywalls (Patreon, Boosty, Ko-fi, private Telegram/Discord channels, and similar platforms). The only exception is strictly standalone translation files (Section 1).
- Collecting funds, donations, or tips in the name of the author (Thistle) or under the guise of funding the development or maintenance of the Synapse project.
- Using mandatory ad-viewing link shorteners or monetized redirects (adf.ly, Linkvertise, and similar services).
- Including the mod or bridge application in paid modpacks or paid compilations.
- Claiming authorship, or removing/altering copyright notices, metadata, version numbers, or credits to the author.
- Publishing modified versions of the mod, bridge, executable files, or assets without the express written consent of the author.
- Using the "Synapse" name, icons, or project branding for third-party projects in a manner that misleads users regarding authorship.
- Uploading the files to platforms where compliance with the above conditions is impossible.

